From: OpenEmbedded <oe@oe-alliance.org>
Date: 2026-04-30
Subject: [PATCH] _ssl: disable removed TLS version-specific methods for OpenSSL 4.0

OpenSSL 4.0 removed the legacy TLS version-specific method functions
(TLSv1_method, TLSv1_1_method, TLSv1_2_method, SSLv3_method).
These functions were deprecated since OpenSSL 1.1.0 and are no longer
present in OpenSSL 4.0.

Python 3.14.4's _ssl.c guards these with OPENSSL_NO_*_METHOD macros,
but OpenSSL 4.0 doesn't define those macros even though the functions
are gone, causing "undefined symbol" errors at runtime.

This is a backport of the fix from CPython PR #146217 (merged 2026-03-25)
which will be included in Python 3.14.5.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/146217]
Signed-off-by: OpenEmbedded <oe@oe-alliance.org>

--- a/Modules/_ssl.c
+++ b/Modules/_ssl.c
@@ -133,6 +133,18 @@
 #else
 #error Unsupported OpenSSL version
 #endif
+
+/* OpenSSL 4.0 removed legacy protocol support and method functions */
+#if (OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x40000000L)
+# define OPENSSL_NO_SSL3
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_1
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_2
+# define OPENSSL_NO_SSL3_METHOD
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_METHOD
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_1_METHOD
+# define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_2_METHOD
+#endif

 /* OpenSSL API 1.1.0+ does not include version methods */
 #ifndef OPENSSL_NO_SSL3_METHOD
